These are audit outcomes, not an intelligence score. A specification-only result means the intellectual machinery is present, but that round did not demonstrate an executable implementation.

The most consequential failure was in the governance test. With equally weighted dimensions and a sample approval threshold of 0.75, an action with safety scored at 0.20 still achieved an aggregate score of 0.80, passing the gate. That configuration is illustrative, not a claim about a deployed policy.

This is precisely the kind of architecture defect the Pantheon’s own Mirror and Hound doctrines are intended to expose.

